1
00:00:00,023 --> 00:00:04,900
In the past years,
no one else stayed with me.

2
00:00:04,901 --> 00:00:07,001
I want to be your wife.

3
00:00:08,041 --> 00:00:09,963
I think it's because he's been too busy.

4
00:00:09,964 --> 00:00:11,599
You haven't had enough sleep

5
00:00:11,599 --> 00:00:13,667
because you're busy preparing
for the premiere night, right?

6
00:00:13,667 --> 00:00:18,284
I'm glad you accepted my offer
to give our friendship a second chance, Liam.

7
00:00:18,284 --> 00:00:20,510
We should communicate to the voters

8
00:00:20,510 --> 00:00:23,492
that I should continue
the good things I've started.

9
00:00:23,492 --> 00:00:24,898
Thank you so much, everyone.

10
00:00:24,898 --> 00:00:28,500
I'm so glad
to see you all happy and complete.

11
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:29,500
What are...

12
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,620
You're the man who's always in my dreams.

13
00:00:32,620 --> 00:00:34,233
I saw I was shot.

14
00:00:34,234 --> 00:00:37,938
I felt that I died.

15
00:00:50,569 --> 00:00:53,105
I saw that I got shot.

16
00:00:54,472 --> 00:00:57,142
I felt that...

17
00:00:57,142 --> 00:00:59,210
I died.

18
00:01:09,821 --> 00:01:11,798
Babe... babe, look at me. Look at me.

19
00:01:11,798 --> 00:01:13,601
What's going on?

20
00:01:13,601 --> 00:01:15,398
Joyce.

21
00:01:16,444 --> 00:01:18,546
I died.

22
00:01:21,023 --> 00:01:25,271
I saw it. I felt that... I died.

23
00:01:25,271 --> 00:01:27,206
Babe, relax.

24
00:01:27,206 --> 00:01:28,708
Don't think about...

25
00:01:28,708 --> 00:01:30,676
Please get her some water.

26
00:01:31,677 --> 00:01:33,679
Miss, please give me some water.

27
00:01:35,514 --> 00:01:37,850
Liam, what's happening?
What did you do to Joyce?

28
00:01:37,850 --> 00:01:41,286
Do you plan to scare her to death?

29
00:01:42,021 --> 00:01:44,724
- I didn't do anything.
- I saw it.

30
00:01:44,724 --> 00:01:47,626
I saw... I saw it like it really happened.

31
00:01:47,626 --> 00:01:51,163
I saw that we were shooting a scene...

32
00:01:51,163 --> 00:01:53,866
I was shot. I died. It felt so real.

33
00:01:53,866 --> 00:01:56,769
I felt that I died.

34
00:01:56,769 --> 00:01:58,498
Babe, have some water first.

35
00:01:58,498 --> 00:02:00,372
Calm down, babe.

36
00:02:02,908 --> 00:02:05,277
Miss Joyce, don't say that.

37
00:02:05,277 --> 00:02:07,079
Knock on wood.

38
00:02:07,079 --> 00:02:10,783
Don't say that.
I'm the one handling the props.

39
00:02:10,783 --> 00:02:12,985
I'm not joking. I'm telling the truth.

40
00:02:12,985 --> 00:02:15,154
I saw it, Liam. You!

41
00:02:15,154 --> 00:02:17,656
You're the man who's always in my dreams.

42
00:02:17,656 --> 00:02:19,525
You're telling me something.

43
00:02:19,525 --> 00:02:24,763
Joyce, I'm... I'm sorry.
But I don't know what you're talking about.

44
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:28,700
What?

45
00:02:29,448 --> 00:02:32,671
Miss Joyce, it's just a dream.

46
00:02:32,671 --> 00:02:35,174
Let's all relax.

47
00:02:35,174 --> 00:02:38,411
Death in a dream might mean,
you know, just the end of something.

48
00:02:38,411 --> 00:02:41,047
Just like our movie that concluded.

49
00:02:41,047 --> 00:02:44,286
And also the beginning of something new.

50
00:02:44,286 --> 00:02:47,253
Maybe we'll have a new project. Right?

51
00:02:47,253 --> 00:02:49,121
New work?

52
00:02:49,121 --> 00:02:51,123
But you said you've been
dreaming of Sir Liam.

53
00:02:51,123 --> 00:02:53,492
Right, Miss Joyce?

54
00:02:54,175 --> 00:02:57,029
What's your interpretation of it, Megan?

55
00:02:57,029 --> 00:02:59,197
I don't want to interpret it.

56
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:05,371
Guys, please.
Can we not get ahead of ourselves?

57
00:03:05,371 --> 00:03:08,274
Should we call a witch doctor?
Someone might have put a curse on you.

58
00:03:08,274 --> 00:03:10,108
It's scary.

59
00:03:12,736 --> 00:03:15,548
I don't know. I feel dizzy.

60
00:03:15,548 --> 00:03:17,382
Dear, is there a problem?

61
00:03:18,484 --> 00:03:19,658
Breathe.

62
00:03:19,658 --> 00:03:21,921
Hey, babe. Baby, look at me.

63
00:03:21,921 --> 00:03:23,243
Babe.

64
00:03:28,559 --> 00:03:29,995
Sorry.

65
00:03:42,774 --> 00:03:44,548
<i>Just like Mom,</i>

66
00:03:44,548 --> 00:03:48,501
<i>she remembers the events I altered
using the typewriter.</i>

67
00:03:49,439 --> 00:03:51,650
<i>You're experiencing it too, Joyce.</i>

68
00:03:51,650 --> 00:03:54,052
<i>Is it because you and Mom are alike?</i>

69
00:04:06,932 --> 00:04:09,601
Was it wrong to change what happened?

70
00:04:19,499 --> 00:04:21,574
What has changed, Liam?

71
00:04:34,892 --> 00:04:37,295
The last time we talked, Liam,

72
00:04:37,295 --> 00:04:41,145
you told me you knew the real reason
behind what happened to Uncle Edmond.

73
00:04:41,145 --> 00:04:44,836
This has to do with
my investigation of Casa Fuerte.

74
00:04:46,138 --> 00:04:47,806
Now, tell me.

75
00:04:47,806 --> 00:04:49,274
Why...

76
00:04:50,641 --> 00:04:52,844
Why did you change your mind?

77
00:04:57,550 --> 00:04:59,545
I'm sorry, Hans.

78
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:03,409
Maybe...

79
00:05:04,886 --> 00:05:08,427
maybe it was just my writer's instinct...

80
00:05:08,427 --> 00:05:12,698
that I want everything
to have an explanation.

81
00:05:12,698 --> 00:05:14,200
First of all, I don't have proof.

82
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:17,335
I might only make things more complicated.

83
00:05:18,733 --> 00:05:20,801
Sorry if...

84
00:05:21,952 --> 00:05:26,423
I put ideas in your head.

85
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:30,115
But I'll leave everything to you for now.

86
00:05:30,115 --> 00:05:34,291
Liam, I can't just ignore what you said.

87
00:05:36,009 --> 00:05:40,192
We're talking about the reason
why my fiancée's father went blind.

88
00:05:42,431 --> 00:05:43,865
Liam.

89
00:05:44,606 --> 00:05:45,874
Liam!

90
00:05:47,119 --> 00:05:49,654
Are you and Liam talking about me?

91
00:05:50,459 --> 00:05:51,860
No, Uncle.

92
00:05:53,239 --> 00:05:54,573
Hans.

93
00:05:57,324 --> 00:05:59,000
Thank you for your concern,

94
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,914
but listen to me carefully.

95
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:09,012
You're marrying my daughter.

96
00:06:09,013 --> 00:06:13,848
You should focus on that.

97
00:06:13,848 --> 00:06:16,754
I want you and Joyce to be happy...

98
00:06:17,463 --> 00:06:19,999
and have a peaceful life.

99
00:06:19,999 --> 00:06:24,536
- Uncle Edmond...
- Promise me this, Hans.

100
00:06:25,771 --> 00:06:29,192
You will protect my daughter.

101
00:06:29,192 --> 00:06:32,177
You will keep her away from harm.

102
00:06:32,177 --> 00:06:34,346
Your job is dangerous.

103
00:06:34,346 --> 00:06:36,114
You know that.

104
00:06:36,963 --> 00:06:41,153
You might be going
against someone influential.

105
00:06:41,153 --> 00:06:44,222
And I don't want my daughter to get involved.

106
00:06:45,395 --> 00:06:46,830
Uncle...

107
00:06:49,128 --> 00:06:51,429
I love your daughter so much.

108
00:06:52,665 --> 00:06:56,676
I will do everything.
I will protect her more than my own life.

109
00:06:56,676 --> 00:06:58,343
I promise you that.

110
00:07:02,274 --> 00:07:06,178
The program is about to start.
Let's go back to our seats.

111
00:07:06,178 --> 00:07:09,083
Go ahead. I'll just get some fresh air.

112
00:07:09,083 --> 00:07:10,778
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

113
00:07:10,778 --> 00:07:12,951
Go on. Go with Joyce.

114
00:07:14,186 --> 00:07:16,621
- Babe...
- Let's go, babe.

115
00:07:21,649 --> 00:07:23,401
Uncle.

116
00:07:27,599 --> 00:07:30,570
<i>I won't come forward, Lando.</i>

117
00:07:30,570 --> 00:07:32,905
<i>Keep my daughter out of this.</i>

118
00:07:32,905 --> 00:07:38,210
<i>The problem, Edmond,
is you know too much.</i>

119
00:07:38,210 --> 00:07:40,479
<i>You see too much.</i>

120
00:07:40,479 --> 00:07:45,044
<i>You should go blind.</i>

121
00:07:45,044 --> 00:07:47,151
<i>Lando, don't!</i>

122
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:49,688
<i>Don't!</i>

123
00:07:53,987 --> 00:07:55,655
Good evening, guys.

124
00:07:56,625 --> 00:08:03,331
I know the success we're enjoying right now
didn't come easy.

125
00:08:04,221 --> 00:08:07,991
We worked hard for this film.

126
00:08:09,672 --> 00:08:12,130
More than that is...

127
00:08:12,130 --> 00:08:14,465
the inspiration that...

128
00:08:15,411 --> 00:08:18,390
our co-workers gave us.

129
00:08:20,365 --> 00:08:25,403
Like the kids in Bahay Aruga Orphanage.

130
00:08:28,918 --> 00:08:30,793
Especially Sep.

131
00:08:30,793 --> 00:08:32,294
Yes!

132
00:08:32,294 --> 00:08:34,129
Sep for the win!

133
00:08:37,223 --> 00:08:38,873
Sir Liam.

134
00:08:38,873 --> 00:08:40,638
Are you okay?

135
00:08:40,638 --> 00:08:45,610
What? Of course. I'm excited to see Sep.

136
00:08:45,610 --> 00:08:46,977
Liam.

137
00:08:48,947 --> 00:08:50,648
That's why...

138
00:08:52,014 --> 00:08:54,650
we offer this celebration...

139
00:08:55,653 --> 00:09:01,225
for the kid who made
the whole production smile.

140
00:09:02,806 --> 00:09:05,375
To Stefano Lualhati,

141
00:09:06,343 --> 00:09:08,078
also known as Sep.

142
00:09:10,835 --> 00:09:13,876
Yes! Go, Sep! That's my boy!

143
00:09:23,712 --> 00:09:25,493
Leroy.

144
00:09:25,493 --> 00:09:28,586
What's going on?
Why are we having this? Where's Sep?

145
00:09:31,298 --> 00:09:33,691
Liam, what's wrong with you?
What are you doing?

146
00:09:33,691 --> 00:09:35,260
Joyce, I don't know where Sep is.

147
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:36,494
- Where's Sep?
- Liam.

148
00:09:36,494 --> 00:09:40,096
- What's happening?
- Liam, that is inappropriate for the kids.

149
00:09:40,096 --> 00:09:42,284
Inappropriate? I'm looking for Sep.
Where is he?

150
00:09:42,284 --> 00:09:44,869
Let's talk later, please.

151
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:49,278
What?

152
00:09:52,385 --> 00:09:53,819
Joy...

153
00:09:58,150 --> 00:10:02,432
Rest in power, Stefano Lualhati.

154
00:10:02,432 --> 00:10:04,589
What? Borj, what are you saying?

155
00:10:04,589 --> 00:10:05,957
What do you mean by that?

156
00:10:05,957 --> 00:10:08,726
What are you talking about?
What's going on?

157
00:10:10,762 --> 00:10:13,030
Liam, sit down first.

158
00:10:22,951 --> 00:10:25,353
Days have gone by so fast.

159
00:10:29,567 --> 00:10:32,669
It has been 40 days since his death.

160
00:10:37,965 --> 00:10:40,067
The reason why...

161
00:10:41,484 --> 00:10:47,423
we celebrate both the success of our film...

162
00:10:48,833 --> 00:10:54,572
and Sep's life,
is because of the deal Liam and I have.

163
00:10:58,239 --> 00:11:00,411
We agreed...

164
00:11:03,966 --> 00:11:08,645
that part of the film's proceeds would go

165
00:11:08,645 --> 00:11:11,513
to the Bahay Aruga Orphanage.

166
00:11:15,816 --> 00:11:17,885
Since that day,

167
00:11:20,238 --> 00:11:25,042
I have the desire in my heart
to help the kids.

168
00:11:32,010 --> 00:11:34,245
I know that...

169
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:38,809
it was a short journey for Sep.

170
00:11:44,131 --> 00:11:47,492
But many people love him.

171
00:11:47,492 --> 00:11:49,158
Joyce... Joyce, wait.

172
00:11:49,158 --> 00:11:50,994
A short journey?

173
00:11:50,994 --> 00:11:52,463
What's this? What is happening?

174
00:11:52,463 --> 00:11:53,501
- Is this a prank?
- Liam.

175
00:11:53,501 --> 00:11:55,002
Are you joking?

176
00:11:55,002 --> 00:11:56,937
- I can't understand.
- Liam, what are you doing?

177
00:11:56,937 --> 00:11:59,150
What am I doing? I'm confused.

178
00:11:59,150 --> 00:12:01,641
I don't know what's going on here.

179
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:05,992
Tell me, what's happening? Where's Sep?

180
00:12:07,815 --> 00:12:09,416
Sister, where's Sep?

181
00:12:09,416 --> 00:12:10,851
Liam, Liam...

182
00:12:10,851 --> 00:12:13,064
Sep is gone, dear.

183
00:12:13,064 --> 00:12:14,687
No... Sister, that's not true.

184
00:12:14,687 --> 00:12:15,989
Sister, don't tell me...

185
00:12:15,989 --> 00:12:17,924
- Sep is not dead!
- Liam!

186
00:12:18,874 --> 00:12:20,898
Sep is already dead.

187
00:12:27,134 --> 00:12:29,641
Please, Liam, calm down.

188
00:12:31,872 --> 00:12:33,674
Liam.

189
00:12:33,674 --> 00:12:35,108
Liam...

190
00:12:35,943 --> 00:12:37,478
I'm sorry.

191
00:12:37,478 --> 00:12:41,781
I don't know what's happening to Liam.
I'm sorry.

192
00:12:53,026 --> 00:12:55,329
No, no, no.

193
00:12:55,329 --> 00:12:57,197
This can't be.

194
00:12:57,197 --> 00:13:01,201
It can't be. Sep can't die. No.

195
00:13:01,201 --> 00:13:03,670
Why can't I remember? Why...

196
00:13:03,670 --> 00:13:07,851
Why do these things happen
whenever I use the typewriter?

197
00:13:09,679 --> 00:13:11,250
No!

198
00:13:12,390 --> 00:13:14,734
Liam, come on!

199
00:13:14,734 --> 00:13:16,898
Liam, calm down!

200
00:13:23,454 --> 00:13:25,158
Joyce.

201
00:13:25,158 --> 00:13:26,860
Joyce, sorry.

202
00:13:27,728 --> 00:13:29,563
Sorry, I don't know anymore.

203
00:13:29,563 --> 00:13:31,665
Liam... What's going on with you?

204
00:13:31,665 --> 00:13:33,901
Make me understand What's happening...

205
00:13:33,901 --> 00:13:35,702
Joyce, I'm confused too.

206
00:13:39,039 --> 00:13:40,240
I don't understand.

207
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:43,744
You told me to celebrate
Sep's 40th day of passing...

208
00:13:43,744 --> 00:13:46,380
You said Sep didn't want us to be sad.

209
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:48,081
What's going on with you?

210
00:13:48,081 --> 00:13:50,383
Joyce, how did Sep die?

211
00:13:52,282 --> 00:13:54,688
Liam, what's with you?
Why don't you seem to remember anything?

212
00:13:54,688 --> 00:13:55,856
Come on!

213
00:13:55,856 --> 00:13:58,057
Tell me, please.

214
00:13:59,199 --> 00:14:01,534
How did Sep die?

215
00:14:04,352 --> 00:14:06,787
Heart failure, Liam.

216
00:14:09,469 --> 00:14:13,706
We've known for a long time
that Sep was sick.

217
00:14:14,990 --> 00:14:17,277
Why wasn't he brought to the hospital?

218
00:14:17,277 --> 00:14:20,647
The doctor talked to the both of us.

219
00:14:23,016 --> 00:14:25,198
Cardiomyopathy.

220
00:14:28,328 --> 00:14:30,870
Sep got it from his father.

221
00:14:32,292 --> 00:14:37,130
Sep was already dead
when the nuns found him.

222
00:14:37,130 --> 00:14:38,898
Does it mean...

223
00:14:42,586 --> 00:14:45,388
Sep died alone?

224
00:14:51,292 --> 00:14:53,661
Sep was alone when he died?

225
00:15:02,758 --> 00:15:04,325
Liam, what...

226
00:15:14,187 --> 00:15:16,795
Son, get up...
It's already late in the morning,

227
00:15:16,795 --> 00:15:19,930
yet your room is still so dark.

228
00:15:19,930 --> 00:15:21,524
Mom.

229
00:15:21,524 --> 00:15:26,045
I thought you would wake up
from the smell of the breakfast I cooked.

230
00:15:27,077 --> 00:15:29,847
Son? I made sure it's good.

231
00:15:29,847 --> 00:15:31,982
Mom, please close the window.

232
00:15:31,982 --> 00:15:33,817
The light is blinding me.

233
00:15:33,817 --> 00:15:36,253
I also feel sad.

234
00:15:40,257 --> 00:15:43,059
I have learned to love Sep, too.

235
00:15:44,862 --> 00:15:46,897
It's so hard, Mom.

236
00:15:49,390 --> 00:15:51,458
I'm having a hard time.

237
00:15:54,838 --> 00:15:58,308
It feels like my heart went numb.

238
00:15:59,777 --> 00:16:01,945
It feels so heavy.

239
00:16:03,447 --> 00:16:06,216
I feel like drowning.

240
00:16:08,852 --> 00:16:10,498
It's so hard to breathe.

241
00:16:13,351 --> 00:16:14,709
Son.

242
00:16:15,726 --> 00:16:21,131
You can't let your heart stop from beating.

243
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:26,691
It's like...

244
00:16:26,691 --> 00:16:31,829
forgetting that Sep existed.

245
00:16:34,977 --> 00:16:38,680
He taught you how to love, didn't he?

246
00:16:41,218 --> 00:16:45,356
So if you keep loving,

247
00:16:45,356 --> 00:16:49,025
Sep continues to live.

248
00:16:53,264 --> 00:16:54,898
Son.

249
00:17:23,921 --> 00:17:26,190
Are you really okay now, Love?

250
00:17:27,564 --> 00:17:29,598
Don't worry about me.

251
00:17:33,984 --> 00:17:37,548
Love, please don't push me away.

252
00:17:37,548 --> 00:17:40,281
I understand.

253
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:46,976
I want to grieve with you.

254
00:17:46,976 --> 00:17:50,245
I know how close you were with Sep.

255
00:17:53,269 --> 00:17:54,870
Thank you.

256
00:17:56,562 --> 00:17:58,829
Look at you. You're still cold.

257
00:17:58,829 --> 00:18:01,498
Can't you be a little sweeter?

258
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:05,967
This is your favorite, right?

259
00:18:05,967 --> 00:18:08,202
I'm not hungry yet.

260
00:18:09,973 --> 00:18:12,009
<i>I got scared.</i>

261
00:18:12,009 --> 00:18:15,246
<i>I only wanted to protect my dad.</i>

262
00:18:15,246 --> 00:18:17,181
I'm the reason...

263
00:18:18,122 --> 00:18:21,392
I'm the reason Joyce died.

264
00:18:22,673 --> 00:18:24,875
How about you, Via?

265
00:18:28,292 --> 00:18:32,462
What's the worst you can do out of hatred?

266
00:18:37,146 --> 00:18:40,048
Love, stop talking that way.

267
00:18:42,610 --> 00:18:45,798
You don't need to be angry with anyone.

268
00:18:46,777 --> 00:18:51,781
We all know that Sep was sick.

269
00:18:52,483 --> 00:18:56,687
<i>But you're the reason
I had to use the typewriter again.</i>

270
00:18:56,687 --> 00:19:01,603
<i>Joyce is alive, but Sep is dead.</i>

271
00:19:01,603 --> 00:19:03,296
<i>I'm sorry, Via,</i>

272
00:19:03,296 --> 00:19:06,396
<i>if I can no longer look at you like before.</i>

273
00:19:08,836 --> 00:19:10,504
Anyway.

274
00:19:11,335 --> 00:19:15,272
I came here to ask

275
00:19:15,272 --> 00:19:18,709
if you can attend the meeting
with Dad tomorrow.

276
00:19:18,709 --> 00:19:20,577
For his campaign?

277
00:19:21,818 --> 00:19:27,524
Honestly, I don't know
why I accepted that project.

278
00:19:30,231 --> 00:19:31,999
That's a no, then.

279
00:19:35,425 --> 00:19:37,419
Don't worry.

280
00:19:37,419 --> 00:19:40,388
I'll just explain it to Dad.

281
00:19:44,067 --> 00:19:45,602
Love.

282
00:19:46,565 --> 00:19:48,878
We're okay, right?

283
00:19:57,074 --> 00:20:01,378
I know you're going through a lot.

284
00:20:03,597 --> 00:20:10,370
I hope you won't let it
affect our relationship.

285
00:20:11,685 --> 00:20:14,587
Please, keep me out of it.

286
00:20:15,277 --> 00:20:18,313
I'm not doing anything wrong.

287
00:20:23,273 --> 00:20:25,975
Isn't that unfair?

288
00:20:28,506 --> 00:20:32,201
You're taking it out on me.

289
00:20:32,201 --> 00:20:34,636
I don't think I deserve that.

290
00:20:47,313 --> 00:20:49,715
Liam, I love you.

291
00:20:53,154 --> 00:20:55,790
I hope you still love me too.

292
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:12,100
[Bahay Aruga Orphanage]

293
00:21:13,813 --> 00:21:16,684
Eat slowly.

294
00:21:16,684 --> 00:21:18,218
Is it good?

295
00:21:21,086 --> 00:21:27,005
Son, are you sure you're okay
to come back here so soon?

296
00:21:27,005 --> 00:21:29,741
You might miss Sep even more.

297
00:21:30,988 --> 00:21:32,556
Mom...

298
00:21:33,848 --> 00:21:36,814
I have learned to love these kids.

299
00:21:38,302 --> 00:21:40,665
And as you said,

300
00:21:41,453 --> 00:21:45,290
as long as my heart is full of love,

301
00:21:46,359 --> 00:21:48,923
I will never forget Sep.

302
00:21:53,251 --> 00:21:56,733
Mama Tess, your spaghetti is so good.

303
00:21:56,733 --> 00:21:58,157
Wow!

304
00:21:58,157 --> 00:21:59,971
Really? Did you like it?

305
00:21:59,971 --> 00:22:02,607
- Yes.
- Oh, thank you!

306
00:22:02,607 --> 00:22:03,908
Go on. Eat some more.

307
00:22:03,908 --> 00:22:06,710
Sir Liam, let's do TikTok.

308
00:22:07,645 --> 00:22:08,779
Sir Liam.

309
00:22:08,779 --> 00:22:10,982
Miss Joyce, let's do TikTok.

310
00:22:10,982 --> 00:22:14,652
Cupid's arrow hit me.

311
00:22:14,652 --> 00:22:18,360
- Are you in love?
- Are you in love?

312
00:22:21,859 --> 00:22:23,404
Sorry, I can't.

313
00:22:28,193 --> 00:22:30,295
I'll do it with you. Is it okay?

314
00:22:30,295 --> 00:22:31,469
Can you teach me how?

315
00:22:31,469 --> 00:22:33,371
- Yes.
- Really? Come on.

316
00:22:33,371 --> 00:22:35,539
I don't know how to do it.

317
00:22:36,173 --> 00:22:37,582
Can you show me? How do we do it?

318
00:22:37,582 --> 00:22:39,143
You do it like this.

319
00:22:41,512 --> 00:22:44,148
Wow! That was good!

320
00:22:44,148 --> 00:22:46,017
Who else knows how to do it?

321
00:22:46,017 --> 00:22:47,524
Come on, let's do TikTok.

322
00:22:47,524 --> 00:22:49,327
I want to see it!

323
00:22:49,327 --> 00:22:51,788
Go on. Please, show me how.

324
00:22:53,031 --> 00:22:54,424
Game!

325
00:23:00,314 --> 00:23:08,167
<i>I want to be near Mom and Dad
when I become a star.</i>

326
00:23:08,167 --> 00:23:10,969
<i>I will watch over you.</i>

327
00:23:12,361 --> 00:23:15,464
<i>I promise Miss Joyce,</i>

328
00:23:15,464 --> 00:23:21,886
<i>your mom, and your dad
that I will watch over you.</i>

329
00:23:21,886 --> 00:23:23,453
<i>Sorry, Sep.</i>

330
00:23:24,220 --> 00:23:29,034
<i>I couldn't fulfill my promise
to take care of you.</i>

331
00:23:29,034 --> 00:23:32,643
<i>Now, you're gone.</i>

332
00:23:32,643 --> 00:23:36,934
<i>I can't even remember
what happened to you.</i>

333
00:23:38,028 --> 00:23:40,204
<i>I'm sorry...</i>

334
00:23:40,204 --> 00:23:43,233
<i>I chose to save Joyce's life.</i>

335
00:23:43,233 --> 00:23:48,693
Sir Liam, I wish I was a star.

336
00:23:48,693 --> 00:23:49,701
Why?

337
00:23:49,701 --> 00:23:56,340
So even if my parents die early,

338
00:23:56,341 --> 00:24:00,524
I would have already spent millions of years
with them.

339
00:24:01,879 --> 00:24:08,032
<i>I don't know
if you're my son's reincarnation.</i>

340
00:24:08,032 --> 00:24:10,301
<i>Is fate playing tricks on me?</i>

341
00:24:10,301 --> 00:24:12,636
<i>I can't understand anymore.</i>

342
00:24:13,270 --> 00:24:16,874
<i>I know you're not Dex.</i>

343
00:24:16,874 --> 00:24:22,895
<i>But I've learned to love you
like my own son, Sep.</i>

344
00:24:35,626 --> 00:24:37,728
Sister.

345
00:24:37,728 --> 00:24:39,975
Have you seen Liam?

346
00:24:39,975 --> 00:24:41,465
No.

347
00:24:41,465 --> 00:24:43,367
Maybe he's here.

348
00:25:00,651 --> 00:25:02,019
Liam?

349
00:25:04,655 --> 00:25:06,356
Joyce?

350
00:25:36,123 --> 00:25:39,046
Mom and I visited the kids.

351
00:25:41,926 --> 00:25:44,928
Sister and I have something to discuss.

352
00:25:50,634 --> 00:25:54,738
I can still hear Sep's laughter in my head...

353
00:25:59,643 --> 00:26:01,800
And his witty remarks.

354
00:26:12,523 --> 00:26:16,393
He will forever be on our minds...

355
00:26:24,735 --> 00:26:27,053
and in our hearts.

356
00:26:38,182 --> 00:26:39,717
Hi, Sister.

357
00:26:39,717 --> 00:26:42,086
- Liam, son. I've been looking for you.
- Aunt Tess.

358
00:26:42,086 --> 00:26:43,420
- Mom.
- Joyce.

359
00:26:43,420 --> 00:26:46,490
Good morning.

360
00:26:46,490 --> 00:26:49,600
So you and Sister are here, Miss Joyce.

361
00:26:49,600 --> 00:26:51,904
Can we start the meeting?

362
00:26:51,904 --> 00:26:53,911
Wait. Meeting?

363
00:26:56,266 --> 00:27:01,631
I want to know
what other assistance the orphanage needs

364
00:27:01,631 --> 00:27:05,092
to make the kids' situation better.

365
00:27:05,092 --> 00:27:07,578
Sister, you wanted to see us?

366
00:27:07,578 --> 00:27:08,812
Yes.

367
00:27:10,412 --> 00:27:13,684
This is Lerna and Arnel. They're a couple.

368
00:27:13,684 --> 00:27:20,190
Lerna is my secretary
and Arnel is our all-around boy.

369
00:27:20,190 --> 00:27:23,893
And this is Liam and Joyce.

370
00:27:23,893 --> 00:27:27,765
They will help us renovate the orphanage.

371
00:27:27,765 --> 00:27:29,800
Really? They're going to help us?

372
00:27:29,800 --> 00:27:34,805
We're so glad to hear that.
We can't do it on our own.

373
00:27:36,072 --> 00:27:41,139
Sister, can you tell us
the estimated cost of the renovation?

374
00:27:41,139 --> 00:27:43,581
It's more or less...

375
00:27:43,581 --> 00:27:45,382
I will help.

376
00:27:45,382 --> 00:27:47,117
And Borj, too.

377
00:27:47,117 --> 00:27:50,053
You need manpower, right?

378
00:27:50,053 --> 00:27:51,589
Of course, Liam.

379
00:27:51,589 --> 00:27:52,723
Okay.

380
00:27:52,723 --> 00:27:56,359
The more help we get, the better.

381
00:27:56,359 --> 00:28:01,147
Okay, I will also tell Deedee and Leroy
while they're not yet busy.

382
00:28:01,148 --> 00:28:05,819
I'll take care of your food.

383
00:28:08,047 --> 00:28:10,227
Thank you so much.

384
00:28:10,227 --> 00:28:12,776
You are heaven-sent.

385
00:28:15,733 --> 00:28:20,651
We can start
as soon as I buy everything we need.

386
00:28:20,651 --> 00:28:22,667
Aren't you busy, dear?

387
00:28:22,668 --> 00:28:33,947
Like I said, I always have time
for you, the kids, and Sep.

388
00:28:46,377 --> 00:28:51,315
Children, enough running.
You might get hurt.

389
00:28:51,315 --> 00:28:53,317
That's enough.

390
00:28:53,317 --> 00:28:55,653
Yes, Sister.

391
00:28:55,653 --> 00:28:59,490
I'm sorry you had to see that, Liam.

392
00:28:59,490 --> 00:29:01,692
It's okay.

393
00:29:01,692 --> 00:29:03,527
Kids are really stubborn.

394
00:29:03,527 --> 00:29:07,398
But it feels good to watch them.

395
00:29:07,398 --> 00:29:09,800
But sometimes they make us
lose our poise.

396
00:29:09,800 --> 00:29:14,015
We earn negative points up there.

397
00:29:17,040 --> 00:29:18,442
I don't know.

398
00:29:18,442 --> 00:29:24,981
I've become anxious since Sep died.

399
00:29:26,654 --> 00:29:33,623
I can't help but remember
the night Sister Pam and I

400
00:29:33,623 --> 00:29:36,559
found him unconscious.

401
00:29:36,559 --> 00:29:40,798
He was gone when we brought him
to the hospital.

402
00:29:43,107 --> 00:29:47,998
I'm sorry if that was such a downer.

403
00:29:47,998 --> 00:29:51,756
If only I could do something for Sep.

404
00:29:51,756 --> 00:29:54,678
I still blame myself for what happened.

405
00:29:54,678 --> 00:29:58,481
Sister, no one wanted it to happen.

406
00:29:59,950 --> 00:30:01,587
I don't know, Liam.

407
00:30:01,587 --> 00:30:05,928
If only we found him earlier.

408
00:30:05,928 --> 00:30:10,351
That night, we heard him screaming.

409
00:30:10,351 --> 00:30:15,099
He sounded like he was fighting with someone.

410
00:30:15,099 --> 00:30:19,536
And when we went out,
we found him on the ground unconscious.

411
00:30:19,536 --> 00:30:21,572
But you know what's puzzling?

412
00:30:21,572 --> 00:30:25,976
When we went out of the gate,
it smelled like gasoline.

413
00:30:25,976 --> 00:30:27,911
Sister.

414
00:30:27,911 --> 00:30:30,656
It smelled like gasoline?

415
00:30:30,656 --> 00:30:34,001
And you found Sep outside unconscious?

416
00:30:48,398 --> 00:30:50,037
Uncle Ramon.

417
00:30:50,037 --> 00:30:51,735
I didn't know you were here.

418
00:30:51,735 --> 00:30:54,437
Sorry, I was busy.

419
00:30:55,565 --> 00:31:01,733
How does it feel to be
the new CEO of Casa Fuerte?

420
00:31:06,250 --> 00:31:09,652
I owe you big time, Uncle Ramon.

421
00:31:12,273 --> 00:31:15,042
Danilo isn't getting any younger.

422
00:31:17,004 --> 00:31:22,566
This office needs a new monster.

423
00:31:22,566 --> 00:31:24,954
Someone hungry.

424
00:31:24,954 --> 00:31:28,190
Someone who wants to prove himself.

425
00:31:30,044 --> 00:31:34,581
Well, Uncle Ramon, I'm your man.

426
00:31:36,678 --> 00:31:38,479
You're the man.

427
00:31:39,645 --> 00:31:41,013
Really?

428
00:31:43,057 --> 00:31:49,396
I wonder why you still
haven't done what I asked you.

429
00:31:50,962 --> 00:31:55,734
To acquire the land of
the Bahay Aruga Orphanage.

430
00:31:55,734 --> 00:31:58,203
Just give me time, Uncle Ramon.

431
00:31:58,203 --> 00:32:00,571
You'll get your hands
on that property eventually.

432
00:32:01,450 --> 00:32:04,075
Make sure of that, Vergil.

433
00:32:04,075 --> 00:32:10,648
I'm not the type of man
who patiently waits to get what he wants.

434
00:32:28,901 --> 00:32:31,200
[Bahay Aruga Orphanage]

435
00:32:46,641 --> 00:32:48,386
Boss Bro!

436
00:32:48,386 --> 00:32:51,089
I thought we'll be on full force?

437
00:32:51,089 --> 00:32:53,491
Looks like we're in trouble.

438
00:32:54,759 --> 00:32:56,775
Are you saying something, Borj?

439
00:32:56,775 --> 00:33:00,434
Megan, if this is filming
and you're the first to arrive,

440
00:33:00,434 --> 00:33:02,633
you'll be complaining, too.

441
00:33:06,086 --> 00:33:07,820
There they are.

442
00:33:16,428 --> 00:33:18,433
Have you started already?

443
00:33:18,434 --> 00:33:19,997
Sorry, Borj.

444
00:33:19,998 --> 00:33:22,052
We first made sure we had all the materials.

445
00:33:22,053 --> 00:33:24,307
And we talked to the kids, too.

446
00:33:24,308 --> 00:33:26,176
They said they are going to help.

447
00:33:27,125 --> 00:33:28,965
The kids are going to help?

448
00:33:28,965 --> 00:33:30,551
How?

449
00:33:30,551 --> 00:33:32,853
Kids!

450
00:33:33,715 --> 00:33:36,968
Come on, let's go downstairs. Careful, okay?

451
00:33:36,968 --> 00:33:38,436
Careful.

452
00:33:38,436 --> 00:33:40,738
Hello!

453
00:33:40,738 --> 00:33:41,973
Are you happy?

454
00:33:41,973 --> 00:33:43,474
Yes!

455
00:33:43,474 --> 00:33:44,576
Are you excited?

456
00:33:44,576 --> 00:33:46,677
Yes!

457
00:33:47,445 --> 00:33:50,148
- Okay, let's go.
- We've got lots of helpers.

458
00:33:50,148 --> 00:33:52,417
Are your hands ready?

459
00:33:52,417 --> 00:33:54,664
Ready?

460
00:33:54,664 --> 00:33:56,421
Be careful, kids.

461
00:33:56,421 --> 00:33:58,689
Don't get too excited.

462
00:33:59,691 --> 00:34:01,258
Careful.

463
00:34:10,535 --> 00:34:12,337
Hey, are you just going
to keep standing there?

464
00:34:12,337 --> 00:34:13,504
Why don't you help us?

465
00:34:13,504 --> 00:34:15,974
Deedee, work the wall.
Leroy, come here.

466
00:34:15,974 --> 00:34:17,942
- Why are you and Leroy together?
- Right, right.

467
00:34:17,942 --> 00:34:20,311
- The wall is too high.
- I should be with Leroy.

468
00:34:20,311 --> 00:34:22,013
Later. Come over here.

469
00:34:22,013 --> 00:34:24,322
You're too happy.

470
00:34:32,623 --> 00:34:35,193
It's not just the kids who are happy.

471
00:34:35,193 --> 00:34:37,662
You made us happy, too.

472
00:34:37,662 --> 00:34:39,830
Anything for the kids.

473
00:34:40,830 --> 00:34:43,780
Anything for Sep's friends.

474
00:34:43,780 --> 00:34:50,340
We want them to learn the value
of helping each other.

475
00:34:50,340 --> 00:34:52,208
When you're home,

476
00:34:52,208 --> 00:34:56,379
there's no one else you can count on
but your family.

477
00:34:56,379 --> 00:34:59,967
You're right, Miss Joyce.
It's not bad to get help.

478
00:34:59,967 --> 00:35:02,482
But like we always do,

479
00:35:02,482 --> 00:35:05,154
we draw strength from each other.

480
00:35:06,389 --> 00:35:07,724
Oh, by the way, Liam,

481
00:35:07,724 --> 00:35:10,858
let's go see that thing you asked me about.

482
00:35:10,858 --> 00:35:12,028
- Okay.
- Let's go.

483
00:35:12,028 --> 00:35:14,209
Where are you going?

484
00:35:14,209 --> 00:35:21,092
Arnel and I will check
what else we have to fix here.

485
00:35:21,092 --> 00:35:24,241
Okay. Don't take too long, okay?
You can't run away from work.

486
00:35:24,241 --> 00:35:27,428
We still have a lot to paint.

487
00:35:27,428 --> 00:35:28,978
Yes, Ma'am.

488
00:35:28,978 --> 00:35:32,415
You don't want to lose sight of him, huh?

489
00:35:35,251 --> 00:35:37,887
We're just friends, Lerna.

490
00:35:37,887 --> 00:35:39,709
Yes. We're just friends.

491
00:35:39,709 --> 00:35:41,920
Okay. If you say so.

492
00:35:41,920 --> 00:35:44,394
Just draw it on the wall.

493
00:35:44,394 --> 00:35:45,961
Hey.

494
00:35:46,609 --> 00:35:47,822
- Come on.
- Let's go.

495
00:35:47,822 --> 00:35:49,281
Babe.

496
00:35:55,836 --> 00:35:57,607
Here. There's CCTV over there.

497
00:35:57,607 --> 00:35:59,180
And there's another one there.

498
00:35:59,180 --> 00:36:02,556
But they are not working.
Both have been defective.

499
00:36:02,556 --> 00:36:05,381
We don't have budget for the repair.

500
00:36:05,381 --> 00:36:07,694
Does it mean it did not capture anything?

501
00:36:07,694 --> 00:36:09,886
Nothing. It's just for display...

502
00:36:09,886 --> 00:36:13,403
To scare off crooks.

503
00:36:14,357 --> 00:36:17,093
They can't get anything
in the orphanage, anyway.

504
00:36:17,093 --> 00:36:20,160
What will they get? Kids?

505
00:36:21,864 --> 00:36:24,756
Sorry, that's not funny.

506
00:36:24,756 --> 00:36:28,792
Why are you interested
in the CCTVs here, Liam?

507
00:36:31,207 --> 00:36:32,575
Nothing.

508
00:36:32,575 --> 00:36:35,645
I just want added security for the orphanage.

509
00:36:35,645 --> 00:36:38,214
Oh. I thought you wanted
to check on something.

510
00:36:38,214 --> 00:36:39,883
But don't worry.
I will ask the village officers

511
00:36:39,883 --> 00:36:43,152
if they can fix the cameras.

512
00:36:49,200 --> 00:36:50,659
Are you okay?

513
00:36:52,729 --> 00:36:55,231
Yes, I'm okay.

514
00:36:55,899 --> 00:36:57,399
Why do you ask?

515
00:37:00,259 --> 00:37:04,207
I just noticed that you're with us,

516
00:37:04,207 --> 00:37:07,176
but your mind is wandering somewhere else.

517
00:37:08,148 --> 00:37:09,900
Is there a problem?

518
00:37:12,749 --> 00:37:14,315
Joyce...

519
00:37:15,385 --> 00:37:18,441
did you know that Sep was found outside?

520
00:37:18,441 --> 00:37:20,909
The nuns found him unconscious.

521
00:37:21,758 --> 00:37:24,660
Sister told me about that.

522
00:37:25,995 --> 00:37:28,831
Why are you suddenly bringing that up?

523
00:37:30,266 --> 00:37:32,602
Nothing.

524
00:37:32,602 --> 00:37:35,437
I just want to know what really happened.

525
00:37:36,573 --> 00:37:38,865
I understand.

526
00:37:42,078 --> 00:37:45,548
It's really not easy to accept things...

527
00:37:45,548 --> 00:37:47,883
especially for Sep...

528
00:37:48,785 --> 00:37:50,686
who died so young.

529
00:37:53,189 --> 00:37:55,124
But Liam, I hope...

530
00:37:56,926 --> 00:38:00,562
I hope this charity we do for the orphanage

531
00:38:00,562 --> 00:38:04,732
may help us accept his death.

532
00:38:06,102 --> 00:38:08,003
Joyce, I'm sorry...

533
00:38:08,854 --> 00:38:12,523
if lately I'm in a somber mood.

534
